### Density assumptions — every row is an estimate for your bottle

The user explicitly approved density estimates on 2026-09-05. These are approximate room-temperature conversions using references around 20–25°C. No lot density has been measured. Published specific gravities are used numerically as approximate g/mL proxies; water-reference and temperature differences are not corrected. Do not claim the same precision for warm 30–35°C stocks.

| Stock | Density used (g/mL, estimated) | Method | Reference |
|---|---:|---|---|
| Ethanol 96% | 0.806 | reference proxy | [ethanol](https://www.merckmillipore.com/INTERSHOP/web/WFS/Merck-SK-Site/cs_CZ/-/EUR/ShowDocument-File?DocumentType=COA&Origin=PDP&ProductSKU=MDA_CHEM-1590100500) |
| Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian | 0.862 | reference proxy | [bergamot](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=7CL24020) |
| Blackcurrant Absolute | 1.022 | carrier only proxy | [dpg](https://doccenter.dow.com/content/dam/internal/documents/117/117-42002-dipropylene-glycol-regular-grade-technical-data-sheet-french.pdf) |
| Hedione | 1.002 | reference proxy | [hedione](https://www.madarcorporation.com/spec-sheets/raw-materials/hedione/Hedione%20-%204507704%20All%20docs.pdf) |
| Lemon FCF oil Sicilian | 0.849 | reference proxy | [lemon](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=7CC24029) |
| Ambrox Super | 0.980 | mixture model with unmeasured solute specific volume | [dpg](https://doccenter.dow.com/content/dam/internal/documents/117/117-42002-dipropylene-glycol-regular-grade-technical-data-sheet-french.pdf), [ipm](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/GB/en/product/aldrich/172472), [ethanol](https://www.merckmillipore.com/INTERSHOP/web/WFS/Merck-SK-Site/cs_CZ/-/EUR/ShowDocument-File?DocumentType=COA&Origin=PDP&ProductSKU=MDA_CHEM-1590100500) |
| Iso E Super | 0.965 | reference proxy | [iso_e](https://www.perfumersworld.com/document-list.php?pro_id=3WY00244&tab=ifra) |
| Cedarwood oil Virginia | 0.955 | reference proxy | [cedar](https://www.pentafineingredients.com/catalog/03-16010) |
| Suederal | 0.965 | reference proxy | [suederal](https://www.perfumersworld.com/document-list.php?pro_id=3UP14351) |
| Habanolide | 0.964 | reference proxy | [habanolide](https://www.industrialchemicals.gov.au/sites/default/files/NA577%20Public%20Report%20PDF.pdf) |
| Allyl Amyl Glycolate | 1.098 | additive specific volume model | [aag](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=4FG00029), [dep](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/524972) |
| Evernyl | 1.120 | carrier only proxy | [dep](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/524972) |
| Cade Oil Rectified | 1.022 | carrier only proxy | [dpg](https://doccenter.dow.com/content/dam/internal/documents/117/117-42002-dipropylene-glycol-regular-grade-technical-data-sheet-french.pdf) |
| Patchouli EO | 0.963 | related grade proxy | [patchouli](https://berjeinc.com/products/patchouli-oil-light/) |
| Schinus molle EO | 0.855 | reference proxy | [schinus](https://berjeinc.com/products/schinus-molle-oil-pink-peppercorn-oil/) |

Reference selection notes:

- Ethanol 0.806 is a working choice within the reference 96% product's d20/20 range 0.805–0.812; it does not identify your ethanol grade or determine its ethanol/water mass split.
- Hedione 1.002 is the rounded midpoint of 0.995–1.008 at 25°C; this is ordinary Hedione, not HC.
- Iso E Super 0.965, Virginia cedar 0.955, and Suederal 0.965 are midpoints of the cited supplier ranges 0.961–0.969, 0.940–0.970, and 0.94–0.99 respectively.
- Habanolide 0.964 is a published reference at 20°C. Patchouli 0.963 is a related-oil density proxy from a 0.950–0.975 range, not a claim that your Aroma&More oil is the supplier's light grade. Schinus 0.855 is the midpoint of the cited 0.830–0.880 range.
- Blackcurrant and Cade use DPG's 1.022 g/mL as first-order stock-density proxies. Evernyl uses DEP's 1.120. The effect of the dissolved material on density is omitted, **not known to be zero**.
- **AAG 10% w/w DEP:** ideal additive specific-volume estimate `1 / (0.10 / 0.935 + 0.90 / 1.120) = 1.09827 g/mL`, using **1.098** for the card. This is not the density of neat AAG and not a DPG-stock conversion.
- **Ambrox 25% w/w custom stock:** `12 / (3 / 1.000 + 7 / 1.022 + 0.5 / 0.850 + 1.5 / 0.806) = 0.97572 g/mL`; coarsely rounded to **0.980**. The 1.000 mL/g apparent specific volume for dissolved Ambrox is an explicit modelling assumption, **not a measured solution or crystal property**. The ethanol component also uses the reference-ethanol proxy. Mixing contraction, dissolution effects and precipitation are not modelled. **Calibrate this stock first if improving the card.**

Calculation: `raw µL = parent stock g × 1000 / estimated stock density`.
Estimated aromatic mass: `raw µL × estimated density / 1000 × w/w fraction`.
Carrier-only proxy estimates and the Ambrox model have unquantified density error; no confidence interval is claimed. For a fixed pipetted volume, a 5% error in the assumed stock density creates a 5% active-mass error before pipette/stock-strength errors. This is a sensitivity example, not a validated error bound.

